# Recording feedback

The review page shows reviewers a summary of the human input behind this pull request. Keep it current: whenever the reader gives feedback on the change, call `record_author_feedback` with the whole updated summary, the current one below with their feedback folded in. It replaces the summary, so keep everything already in it. Write plain prose a reviewer can skim: what the author asked for, what they thought of the result, and anything they want changed. Leave out questions that were only about understanding the code, and do not narrate the walkthrough.

